      "reason": "No explicit statement of the review objective(s) or question(s) is provided in the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "Inclusion criteria of studies: study design: randomized controlled trials; population: patients with Bell ' s palsy (Facial paralysis or idiopathic facial paralysis or herpetic facial paralysis); intervention: the intervention was acupuncture therapy, the acupuncture therapy refers to needling or needling combined with moxibustion; Comparison: oral medication or topical injection without other therapy.",
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence specifies key planned comparisons (acupuncture vs oral medication/topical injection) and identifies the population, but it is not framed as an explicit PICO-style comparison plan beyond inclusion criteria, so completeness relative to the checklist item is unclear."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 55
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "Inclusion criteria of studies: study design: randomized controlled trials; population: patients with Bell ' s palsy (Facial paralysis or idiopathic facial paralysis or herpetic facial paralysis); intervention: the intervention was acupuncture therapy, the acupuncture therapy refers to needling or needling combined with moxibustion; Comparison: oral medication or topical injection without other therapy. Exclusion criteria of studies: not RCTs; trials testing other forms of acupuncture, such as laser acupuncture or electric acupuncture; studies of comparison of 2 different forms of acupuncture methods; the intervention group of studies combined more than 2 therapies, such as acupuncture plus medication.",
      "reason": "Eligibility criteria used to determine eligibility are specified for study design, population, intervention, and comparison. Follow-up/observation timing is partially described elsewhere (\"observation time points...between1to1.5months\" in text_10), but other required components (e.g., settings) are not clearly specified in the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "All the included studies were performed in China and publishedfrom1996to2015.NinestudieswerewritteninChinese and2inEnglish.",
      "reason": "The review specifies dissemination year range (1996 to 2015) and language (Chinese, English). Publication or report status (e.g., published vs unpublished/gray literature) is only indirectly addressed (search without gray literature), but the criterion about eligibility criteria for report characteristics is not fully satisfied based on the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not state that the review distinguishes exclusions due to outcomes not being measured versus exclusions due to outcome results not being reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "The patients were randomly assigned to intervention group (acupuncture group) or control group (drug group), with their age ranging from 8 to 78 years old. In the intervention group, acupuncture treatment only included manual acupuncture or manual acupuncture combined with moxibustion, while the control group only included drugs (oral or injection).",
      "reason": "The evidence defines the groups (acupuncture group vs drug group) and the corresponding comparisons used in the included studies. However, it does not clearly specify how these groups were linked to each synthesis step (e.g., explicit synthesis group definitions for each meta-analysis), beyond indicating subgroup analyses."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Then 20 articles were excluded: 13 were not RCTs, 4 meta-analyses and 3 reviews. Among the left 26 articles, 15 studies with mixed interventions did not meet our inclusion criteria and were excluded: in 3 articles, [24 - 26] the control group combined with non-drug therapy; in 6 articles, non-acupuncture therapy was used in the observation group; in 2 studies, [27,28] the intervention of the observation group was acupuncture plus electroacupuncture; 1 study, [29] used light irradiation therapy device; 2 studies [29,30] used cupping therapy; and the acupuncture group of 1 study [31] used drug therapy. Four studies [32 - 35] compared the effectiveness of different types of acupuncture therapy. The ef fi cacy evaluation of 1 article [36] is not clear, and 1 article. [37] was repeated with the previous study.",
      "reason": "The evidence provides reasons for excluding studies (e.g., not RCTs, mixed interventions, non-matching acupuncture forms/comparators, unclear efficacy, duplicates). However, it does not clearly explain rationales for any notable restrictions beyond enumerating exclusion reasons."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 66
}

